aripiprazole, quetiapine, ziprasidone, or lithium, or anticonvulsants such as carbamazepine and
sodium valproate.
According to a recent meta-analysis, antipsychotics, especially risperidone, haloperidol and
olanzapine (not among options) are recommended as first-line treatment of acute mania in bipolar
disorder both in pregnant and nonpregnant patients.
Lithium can be used as well and is the most appropriate option among others, considering the fact
that at 20 weeks gestation (second trimester) fetal cardiogenesis has already taken place and the
risk of cardiac anomalies, a feared adverse outcome of lithium on the developing fetus, is minimal
if any.
Reportedly, lithium use during the first trimester of pregnancy has been associated with
cardiovascular anomalies (e.g. Epstein’s anomaly), midfacial defects, and other defects;
nonetheless, the benefits to the mother substantially outweigh the risks of fetal anomaly.
Lithium is even safer during the second and third trimesters when cardiogenesis has already
occurred and the risk of fetal malformations is significantly decreased. Lithium requirements
increase in the third trimester; however, dose reduction by 25% is recommended before delivery to',NULL,'Retain the source-era answer for question-bank study; verify current Australian guidance before clinical use.',NULL,NULL,'2023','v2.9.4',1,'text','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-c516f0d5a3f0","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d0d807e340d86565d8d7","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1562,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,'needs_verification','[]','high') ON CONFLICT(id) DO UPDATE SET source_id=excluded.source_id,source_question_no=excluded.source_question_no,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,system=excluded.system,topic=excluded.topic,clinical_task=excluded.clinical_task,stem_en=excluded.stem_en,answer_key=excluded.answer_key,source_explanation_en=excluded.source_explanation_en,memory_rule_en=excluded.memory_rule_en,image_ref=excluded.image_ref,source_year=excluded.source_year,import_version=excluded.import_version,active=1,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk;
