o remove the fear response of a phobia, and substitute a relaxation response to\nthe conditional stimulus gradually using counter conditioning. There are three phases to the\ntreatment:\nPhase 1 - The patient is taught a deep muscle relaxation technique and breathing exercises, e.g.,\ncontrol over breathing, muscle de-tensioning or meditation. This step is very important because of\nreciprocal inhibition, where once response is inhibited because it is incompatible with another. In\nthe case of phobias, fears involves tension and tension is incompatible with relaxation.\nPhase 2 - The patient creates a fear hierarchy starting at stimuli that create the least anxiety (fear)\nand building up in stages to the most fear provoking images. The list is crucial as it provides a\nstructure for the therapy. The following table is an example rated by a patient:\nBehavior\nFear rating\nThink about a dog\n10\nLook at the photo of a dog\n20\nLook at a real dog while\ndetained\n40\nLook at a real dog while\nunleashed\n50\nLook at the dog while it is\napproaching\n60\nLet the dog get close to you\n70\nPat the dog\n80","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["age","guideline","therapy","treatment"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"614defaedaea9070478df3836a793d04395aa74b","duplicate_group_id":"exact-614defaedaea","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d75c2e795909b0d4bcda","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1635,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.