Paradoxic motion of the rib cage and abdomen','{"source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","supporting_pages":[],"source_qid":null,"duplicate_group_id":"exact-6f7acfa56e24","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b14633957277a1e7aea2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1783,"source_qid":null}],"parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","visual_asset":null,"asset_preview_url":null}',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'needs_verification','[]','medium','{"record_id":"b14633957277a1e7aea2","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_year":2023,"source_page":1783,"source_qid":null,"domain_hint":"Mixed/Unclassified","stem":"A 57-year-old man presents to the emergency department with severe shortness of breath and\ntachypnea. As a part of emergency evaluation, an arterial blood gas (ABG) analysis is performed,\nthe result of which are as follows:\nPH: 7.2 (normal 7.35-7.45)\nPaCo2: 48 (normal 35-45 mmHg)\nPaO2: 50 (normal 80 -100 mmHg)\nWhich one of the following is the next best step in management?","options":{"A":"100% oxygen by Hudson mask.","B":"28% oxygen by Venturi mask.","C":"Intubation and ventilation.","D":"Positive pressure ventilation.","E":"Oxygen 6 litres/minute by nasal prongs."},"source_answer":"D","source_explanation":"In case of respiratory failure, oxygen supplementation is the next best step in management. This\ncan be achieved either by high concentration oxygen through nasal cannulae, simple face mask,\nreservoir masks or non-rebreathing masks in type I (hypoxemic respiratory failure) or low-\nconcentration oxygen through Venturi mask in type II (hypercarbic) respiratory failure or for those\npatient at increased risk of type II respiratory failure.\nAs a rule, however, patients with the following conditions should be supported with assisted\nmechanical ventilation, either with non-invasive measures (CPAP, BiPAP) (preferred option) or\nconventional intubation or mechanical ventilation as the last resort if there is:\npersistent or worsening hypoxemia despite supplemental oxygen or inability to achieve an O2\nsaturation above 90% OR\nWorsening hypercapnia (PaCO2>50 mmHg) OR\nWorsening respiratory acidosis (PH<7.25) OR\nClinical manifestations of respiratory distress such as:\nSevere dyspnea\nTachypnea (RR>30)\nNasal flaring\nAccessory muscle use\nTracheal tugging\nRecession of suprasternal and intercostal spaces\nPulsus paradoxus\nDiaphoresis\nParadoxic motion of the rib cage and abdomen","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"medium","currentness_keywords":["age","management"],"likely_visual_question":false,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"6f7acfa56e241766febb01dfe3f9554384685f90","duplicate_group_id":"exact-6f7acfa56e24","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"b14633957277a1e7aea2","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1783,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evid