has been\noverexposed to asbestos. It is important for physicians to become familiar with the operating\nconditions that are associated with potential asbestos exposure. This is particularly important in\nevaluating medical and work histories and in performing physical examinations.\nThe current recommendations include taking a complete history, performing physical exam with\nclose attention to respiratory system and the following diagnostic measures:\n \nChest X-ray – A chest X-ray should be taken for all patients with exposure to asbestos;\nhowever, initially, the chest X-rays are often inconclusive because it takes approximately 3-\n5 years for radiographic signs of asbestos exposure to be evident on X-rays. It is\nrecommended that chest X-rays be repeated at 3-5 years intervals.\nPulmonary function tests (PFTs) – simple PFTs available at general practice level should be\napplied to recognize the possible restrictive patterns caused by asbestosis.\nIf the condition is work-related, involvement of a respiratory or occupational physician is needed to\nconsider factors such as the effect of the exposure on other workers, how to control the exposure\nat the workplace and appropriate use of personal protective equipment.\nWhen a current worker has been identified to have been overexposed to asbestos, measures taken\nby the employer to eliminate or mitigate further exposure should also lower the risk of serious long-\nterm consequences. The employer is required to institute a medical surveillance program for all\nemployees who are or will be exposed to asbestos at or above the permissible exposure limit (0.1\nfiber per cubic centimeter of air).","source_answer_status":"present","current_answer":null,"current_answer_status":"needs_verification","current_evidence":[],"currentness_risk":"high","currentness_keywords":["interval","screen","screening"],"likely_visual_question":true,"parser_confidence":"high","parser_mode":"strict_ocr_tolerant","text_method":"native","parser_version":"2.7.1-parser-only-conservative-staging-2026-09-22","stem_hash":"843e17b17264fd763f78e53a8acece05dd3279dc","duplicate_group_id":"exact-843e17b17264","duplicate_sources":[{"record_id":"d3c95579a769fbf350ee","record_type":"text_mcq","source_file":"Amedex 2023.pdf","source_relative_path":"AMEDEX2025+redbook+handbook图片题/Amedex 2023.pdf","source_page":1818,"source_qid":null}]}',1,'v2.9.4','2026-09-24T00:00:00.000Z') ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET source_file=excluded.source_file,source_page=excluded.source_page,domain=excluded.domain,stem=excluded.stem,options_json=excluded.options_json,source_answer=excluded.source_answer,source_explanation=excluded.source_explanation,provenance_json=excluded.provenance_json,visual_asset=excluded.visual_asset,visual_url=excluded.visual_url,options_mode=excluded.options_mode,current_answer=excluded.current_answer,current_answer_status=excluded.current_answer_status,current_evidence_json=excluded.current_evidence_json,currentness_risk=excluded.currentness_risk,record_json=excluded.record_json,active_quiz=excluded.active_quiz,import_version=excluded.import_version,imported_at=excluded.imported_at;
